course: dictionary
lesson: 4674
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. The word holiday is a good example. A holiday can be a day when school and work stop, a trip away for fun and rest, or a long time off school, like the summer holidays.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Holidays cost more in school holiday weeks because many families want them then; £1,200 − £800 = £400 more.» Here holiday means a time off school, because the sentence talks about school holiday weeks, not a trip.
explain: «Before the car, Toad tries a horse-drawn caravan holiday.» This holiday is a trip away from home, for fun and rest. Swap in your meaning and check: a trip away makes sense here, and so does a time off school.
fact: Holiday is a noun, and the plural is holidays.
fact: A holiday can be a day when people do not go to school or work, like a public holiday.
fact: A holiday can also be a trip you take for fun and rest, away from home. In American English this is called a vacation.
fact: The holidays means a longer time off school, like the summer holidays.
fact: In British English, holiday can also be a verb, which means to spend a holiday somewhere.
exercise: «Holidays cost more in school holiday weeks because many families want them then; £1,200 − £800 = £400 more.» What does the sum show? | Holidays are £800 more | Holidays cost £1,200 in total | Families want less money | *Holidays are £400 more in school holiday weeks
exercise: «Before the car, Toad tries a horse-drawn caravan holiday.» What is a holiday here? | A long time off school in summer | A day when people go to work | *A trip away from home for fun and rest | A day when school is closed for a special event
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means a longer time off school. | holiday homework | on holiday | public holiday | *the summer holidays
test: Which phrase means a day when many people do not work, often for a special event? | the summer holidays | holiday homework | *a public holiday | go on holiday
test: In American English, what word means the same as a holiday trip? | homework | summer | holiday clubs | *vacation
exam: In «Holidays cost more in school holiday weeks», what does holiday mean? | *A time off school | A day to pack a suitcase | A trip to the beach | A public day for a special event
